  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 5.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Morning, um, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.14,
      "end_seconds": 14.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "that's fine, sit down tell me why you came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.14,
      "end_seconds": 26.46,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "um, so... ringing in my left ear that's why I came i've been reading about it it online and it worried me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.21,
      "end_seconds": 30.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "so, how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.53,
      "end_seconds": 54.27,
      "duration_seconds": 22.74,
      "text": "Honestly, every other day. Oh, and numbness on the left cheek. That's been about the same, three days. Oh, I've had gradual hearing loss on the left too, for three days. With gradual hearing loss on the left, maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.13,
      "end_seconds": 58.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.12,
      "end_seconds": 74.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.63,
      "end_seconds": 99.15,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "okay: SpO2 99 percent on room air, temperature 36.9, blood pressure 112 over 69, pulse is 73 beats a minute have you noticed discharge, ear pain or vertigo?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.98,
      "end_seconds": 103.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.92,
      "end_seconds": 107.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "So, any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.89,
      "end_seconds": 111.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "nothing there, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.48,
      "end_seconds": 115.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "And And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.16,
      "end_seconds": 121.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "no, skin's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.18,
      "end_seconds": 126.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.29,
      "end_seconds": 141.59,
      "duration_seconds": 14.3,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I walk the dog every morning. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.72,
      "end_seconds": 152.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "right, anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.53,
      "end_seconds": 157.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I had my septum straightened in my thirties"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.3,
      "end_seconds": 171.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.59,
      "end_seconds": 179.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "I'm on Seretide inhaler, twice a day for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.82,
      "end_seconds": 184.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.02,
      "end_seconds": 200.16,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "I have asthma. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.03,
      "end_seconds": 207.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "okay, go on okay, I can see asthma in your file as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.39,
      "end_seconds": 224.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.46,
      "end_seconds": 227.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.2,
      "end_seconds": 233.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.77,
      "end_seconds": 237.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.82,
      "end_seconds": 253.38,
      "duration_seconds": 14.56,
      "text": "okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: This is probably one-sided nerve hearing loss needing a scan the reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.93,
      "end_seconds": 255.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.15,
      "end_seconds": 268.55,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with one-sided nerve hearing loss needing a scan do well once it's treated properly. We should do a hearing test for unilateral hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.6,
      "end_seconds": 271.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.05,
      "end_seconds": 298.04,
      "duration_seconds": 24.99,
      "text": "one-sided tinnitus with hearing loss always gets a scan, it's usually benign if it hasn't settled next month, we'd think about an MRI of the internal auditory canals, but not now keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency we'll catch up after the scan"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.02,
      "end_seconds": 300.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Yes, that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.11,
      "end_seconds": 306.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.95,
      "end_seconds": 311.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "hmm, alright, thanks, take care"
    }
  ]
}